{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes","id":1205626,"title":"Questions on Nodes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-11T09:13:45-07:00","id":1205626,"title":"Questions on Nodes","content":"- Are there Nodes outside of the mundane realm? So is it possible to harvest Quintessence while inside of a dream realm, like your Demesne? Can your Demesne Background be linked to your Node Background, for example? The idea would be that your dream realm occupies a point of power within the Maya. And the same applies to the Low Umbra, Middle Umbra, High Umbra. And if a Mage is creating their own Realm, can they make the Realm a Node, or add Nodes to it?<br /> <br /> - Is it okay to make your Laboratory or Sanctum the same place as your Node? It makes sense mechanically and thematically, like a Technocrat building their laboratory complex over a node so that they can gradually change the resonance and harvest it (naturally pissing off any associated Mages or Werewolves of course).<br /> <br /> - Mechanically speaking, what does the level of a Node/Cairn actually mean? So what's the difference between a level 1 node and a level 3 node for a Mage with Prime? Furthermore, the difficulty modifiers for working around a Node... I'm assuming that you need to have a matching Paradigm?<br /> <br /> - The Ventures of Primal Utility are Nodes, essentially. Can the energy be harvested by other Mages? So a conglomerate HQ which is bursting with Quintessence, can it be stolen by Mages with mystical paradigms? Does this make it vulgar, or demand a greater level of Prime?<br /> <br /> - Are there mechanics for upgrading Nodes? For example, if a lab is a node, does deepening the academic and scientific excellence of the lab, pouring more Quintessence into it, tapping the wellspring etc. eventually push it up a level? If a Node is filled with a violent resonance, would arranging a violent confrontation at the node help to strengthen it? And along the same thread, can a node be weakened or destroyed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-11-2018, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:36:32-07:00","id":1205661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes#post1205626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Are there Nodes outside of the mundane realm? So is it possible to harvest Quintessence while inside of a dream realm, like your Demesne? Can your Demesne Background be linked to your Node Background, for example? The idea would be that your dream realm occupies a point of power within the Maya. And the same applies to the Low Umbra, Middle Umbra, High Umbra. And if a Mage is creating their own Realm, can they make the Realm a Node, or add Nodes to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine so. Masters of the Art made mention of Archmasters moving their Nodes out into pocket Realms, so they didn't have to bother with defending locations on the material plane. Presumably, various locations in the Umbra may be places of power. That said, such places will probably already have &quot;owners&quot;. Spirits have desire for such resources, too.<br /> <br /> I would not allow a Demesne to host a Node. Sounds like the sort of thing a player would try to do to get away with having a Quintessence source that couldn't be touched. On the other hand, one could easily argue that while a Node in a Demesne might be safe from attack from the material side, it's open to assault from residents of the dreamlands. My problem is that while that could create conflict, defenses mounted around one character's Demesne wouldn't be so exciting for an entire Cabal of PCs. Not everyone could join in, like would happen with an Earthly Node. Not unless everyone had Mind 3.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I find it compelling the idea of venturing out into the dreamlands with Mind 3, and gathering wisps of Quintessence like one would gather wild mushrooms or blackberries. The same could be said of the rest of the Umbra, which could play host to Quintessence gathering missions. Specific parts of the non-material world would have their own flavors of Quintessence, with their own Resonances. Whole stories could be spun from searches for Quintessence with specific, rare Resonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Is it okay to make your Laboratory or Sanctum the same place as your Node? It makes sense mechanically and thematically, like a Technocrat building their laboratory complex over a node so that they can gradually change the resonance and harvest it (naturally pissing off any associated Mages or Werewolves of course). </div> </div> </div>It's not only okay, I imagine it's standard procedure for mages who are in a position to do so. It's why Chantries are often built around Nodes, as a Chantry is somewhat like a Sanctum. Those individual mages with private Nodes have incentive to build their Sanctum around them, not just for the convenience of having their work space on top of a place of power, but because they are in the best position to defend that Node with their full magickal might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Mechanically speaking, what does the level of a Node/Cairn actually mean? So what's the difference between a level 1 node and a level 3 node for a Mage with Prime? Furthermore, the difficulty modifiers for working around a Node... I'm assuming that you need to have a matching Paradigm? </div> </div> </div>Each dot of Node provides X points of Quintessence per week, half as &quot;free&quot; Quintessence and half as Tass. The value of 'X' is determined by the Storyteller, as a function of their decision for how powerful a campaign should be. It can be as low as 2 per dot per week for a gritty street level game (where magical resources are scarce and precious, and every Node is a heavily guarded treasure), or as high as 5 to 10 per dot per week for a high fantasy game (where things like Realms are easy to maintain, spells get thrown around gregariously, and Wonders are relatively cheap to make).<br /> <br /> I imagine the difficulty modifiers are affected, not by Paradigm (Nodes don't really care), but by <i>Resonance</i>. A Node with bloody, violent Resonance will make violent magick easier, but life-affirming and peaceful magick harder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The Ventures of Primal Utility are Nodes, essentially. Can the energy be harvested by other Mages? So a conglomerate HQ which is bursting with Quintessence, can it be stolen by Mages with mystical paradigms? Does this make it vulgar, or demand a greater level of Prime? </div> </div> </div>I don't think a mage not working with Primal Utility can derive Quintessence from a Venture. While a Venture has some qualities as a Node, it's not exactly the same. A Node is a weak spot in the Tellurian, where the energy of creation seeps out. A Venture is more like a system for drawing excess Quintessence out of the people involved in it, and from their activity. The Quintessence only flows into a concentrated form when the Hypereconomist draws it out. The mystic likely wouldn't even notice what was happening, or would only see it as a curious manner in which Patterns interacted with each other. Only when the Syndicate op went to &quot;collect&quot; would the mystic realize what was going on.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine, in any case, that Ventures represent a magickal (or rather Enlightened) exploit that is inextricably tied to the Alternative Sphere of Primal Utility. If you don't understand reality in that way - if you don't also have Primal Utility, rather than Prime - you can't do anything with it. Not unless you found some sort of Rote that uses conjunctional Spheres as a workaround, or even somehow expanded your understanding of Prime so that it gains qualities usually reserved for Primal Utility. The latter would require a fairly fundamental change to a mystic's Paradigm, and not something a Storyteller ought to just let a player handwave away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Are there mechanics for upgrading Nodes? For example, if a lab is a node, does deepening the academic and scientific excellence of the lab, pouring more Quintessence into it, tapping the wellspring etc. eventually push it up a level? If a Node is filled with a violent resonance, would arranging a violent confrontation at the node help to strengthen it? And along the same thread, can a node be weakened or destroyed? </div> </div> </div>To my knowledge, there are no rules for strengthening Nodes. The game tends to treat them as static fixtures, their only changes up to Storyteller fiat.<br /> <br /> Going by my gut, I would not allow playing to Resonance to make a Node stronger. If it were so, I imagine the various sects of the world would prioritize making their Nodes stronger through this method, and there wouldn't be any Nodes controlled by the sects that were &quot;weak&quot;. There'd be too much advantage in playing to Resonance, even if it takes lots of time and effort.<br /> <br /> Rather, I imagine that if it were possible to make a Node more powerful - to increase its dot rating - it would require Prime 5 magick, and probably a great deal of successes. If Prime 5 can be used to make Nodes, it can probably be used to make existing ones bigger. This would make it possible, but not easy or common. (You have to have a Prime Master to do it, and those guys tend to have other stuff they want to be doing that just upgrading all the Nodes. Plus, that kind of thing is Vulgar, which Masters get reluctant about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:40:35-07:00","id":1205664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes#post1205626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Are there Nodes outside of the mundane realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition, no. However Nodes are not the be all and end all of such things. Wellsprings could occur anywhere, including the Umbra or Maya, but are less predictable than Nodes are. Generally, combining the Node Background with Demense or other Realms means the mage has actually linked a Node in the Earthly Realm to their external bastion to access it's power in either location.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it would be reasonable from a strictly mechanical sense to use the Node Background to represent a Demense or Umbral Realm with a high rate of Wellsprings or Junctures (esp, if purposefully created that way through use of various skills and Prime).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Is it okay to make your Laboratory or Sanctum the same place as your Node? </div> </div> </div>Yes, though most mages will prefer to share a Node through a Chantry and have multiple Sanctums on the same Node to maximize the benefits for multiple mages. This is SOP for the Technocracy and common place for other mages out of the need for mutual cooperation and defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Mechanically speaking, what does the level of a Node/Cairn actually mean? </div> </div> </div>The rating dictates the amount of Tass and Quintessence that can safely be harvest from the Node over a period of time.<br /> <br /> For Caerns, using the WtA mechanics, it also dictates the size of the area of influence of the Caern, the approximate number of werewolves that reside there, and the level of spiritual upkeep needed to appease the spirits that empower a Caern beyond just being an energy source (this is how it also predicts the number of Garou, since it can only provide so much energy, and their pacts require upkeep, there's a cost/benefit balance of numbers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, the difficulty modifiers for working around a Node... I'm assuming that you need to have a matching Paradigm? </div> </div> </div>No. Generally speaking the benefits from Nodes in this regard are universal because Nodes are areas of mutable reality from the different Realms mingling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The Ventures of Primal Utility are Nodes, essentially. Can the energy be harvested by other Mages? So a conglomerate HQ which is bursting with Quintessence, can it be stolen by Mages with mystical paradigms? Does this make it vulgar, or demand a greater level of Prime? </div> </div> </div>This isn't really specified, but I would rule that raiding a Venture requires at least a thorough understanding of Hypereconomics on top of the normal Prime rules for such things. The Quintessence generated by Ventures is something that requires either Primal Utility or at least significant understanding of the theories behind it to interact with. Vulgarity and level of Prime would depend on approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Are there mechanics for upgrading Nodes? </div> </div> </div>No, though you've suggested plenty of reasons to allow the Background to be increased over play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:46:40-07:00","id":1205669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes#post1205626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Are there Nodes outside of the mundane realm? So is it possible to harvest Quintessence while inside of a dream realm, like your Demesne? Can your Demesne Background be linked to your Node Background, for example? The idea would be that your dream realm occupies a point of power within the Maya. And the same applies to the Low Umbra, Middle Umbra, High Umbra. And if a Mage is creating their own Realm, can they make the Realm a Node, or add Nodes to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nodes are used as anchors to make realms accessible. The downside is, the quintessence is most likely used up by that particular Node. It may be possible to find other sources of Quintessence, though. (Think of Matter, Epherma, Gnosis and Glamour as different forms of Quintessence and how it would be possible to access these. Glamour, as a free source of energy should be very easy to channel.)<br /> I don't think there are Nodes in the Umbra, as there are different ways for Quintessence to flow through these realms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Is it okay to make your Laboratory or Sanctum the same place as your Node? It makes sense mechanically and thematically, like a Technocrat building their laboratory complex over a node so that they can gradually change the resonance and harvest it (naturally pissing off any associated Mages or Werewolves of course). </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's how I would do it. The only reason to *not* have your Sanctuary directly where the Node is, would be that the Node is very hard to access, like high up the mountains. But who's gonna protect that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Mechanically speaking, what does the level of a Node/Cairn actually mean? So what's the difference between a level 1 node and a level 3 node for a Mage with Prime? Furthermore, the difficulty modifiers for working around a Node... I'm assuming that you need to have a matching Paradigm? </div> </div> </div>It basically means how much Quintessence it generates per week and how much other people may want to take it from you. It's just the mechanical meassure of how strong it is. Also, don't overload your Nodes by draining them of Quintessence constantly.<br /> I'd guess the background Quintessence would make all kinds of magic(k) easier to cast, however it should match the Nodes resonance.<br /> <br /> Just an idea: Linking the power of Resonances around that Node directly to the Nodes level. So a Level 4 Node would manifest it's Resonances on levels of 4. Makes these places of power even weirder and more mystically (or more static, if it's a Technocracy Node).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The Ventures of Primal Utility are Nodes, essentially. Can the energy be harvested by other Mages? So a conglomerate HQ which is bursting with Quintessence, can it be stolen by Mages with mystical paradigms? Does this make it vulgar, or demand a greater level of Prime? </div> </div> </div>It could only be stolen by someone with an appropriate paradigm and stealing the Quintessence of a Venture would basically be stealing a lot of money. Sure, someone of the Hermetic Order might do this, but I doubt a Verbena could access this form of Quintessence since it basically doesn't exist in her Paradigm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Are there mechanics for upgrading Nodes? For example, if a lab is a node, does deepening the academic and scientific excellence of the lab, pouring more Quintessence into it, tapping the wellspring etc. eventually push it up a level? If a Node is filled with a violent resonance, would arranging a violent confrontation at the node help to strengthen it? And along the same thread, can a node be weakened or destroyed? </div> </div> </div>Haven't read anything directly. No mechanics that I know of. But basically Nodes seem to be tiny openings in the gauntlet where Quintessence pours through into our world, from the Flux. It should theoretically be possible to &quot;make it bigger&quot;. Most likely it would also flood the surroundings with that Nodes resonances even more. If you make that violent Node stronger, think about what could happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:32:11-07:00","id":1205756,"title":"","content":"While having a node in the umbra is a arguable feat, it is sure possible to make a prime straw that sucks prime out of a real node.. but those kind of straws are kind of bright and may attract unwanted entities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","user":"RandyRando","date":".  typo 04-11-2018, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T17:11:40-07:00","id":1205830,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses everyone! Cool ideas on the more esoteric stuff not covered in the rules, solid info on the RAW stuff.<br /> <br /> More Questions!<br /> <br /> - Can a Demesne be someone's Sanctum? So I'm imagining someone having a Demesne 5 + Sanctum 5 background where their Memory Palace is extremely powerful and has been shaped to suit their magick. Since Dreams, Invocations, Meditation etc. make up the majority of their foci, the Mage can enter their Demesne while meditating or sleeping and use Magick from inside of it, targeting the real world via Correspondence. Furthermore, when they are in a Sanctum, a Mage gets hidden by the Arcane effect; if a Mage's sanctum is a space in the dream world that they can access, is it arcane in terms of people trying to find it? And does the Mage become Arcane while they're using it?<br /> <br /> - Assuming a Mage has a lot of power over their Demesne (it's their Wellspring, Sanctum and base of operations, and it's also home to a society of Dream-Mind Patterns they created using Mind and Spirit, and they have the lucid dreaming ability at 5 with a spec in Demesne), can it make an effective Mind Prison for enemies? There's a mechanic for dragging people in; once they're there, can you have the dream completely smother them and present them with Things Man Was Not Meant to See (you don't have to experience those, just drag them from the nightmares of Marauders you've extracted without experiencing perhaps?)?<br /> <br /> - Sanctums make all of your Paradigm's effects Coincidental. Considering this, doesn't it make a lot of problems just non-issues? Like the 9 point degeneration flaw, which gives you Aggravated damage each fortnight. With a Sanctum, the roll to fix it is pretty standard. Life 3, Coincidental. And what about effects which are only balanced because of how thoroughly vulgar they are? Like reaching out with Correspondence and turning someone into something nasty (assuming this fits the lab/sanctum). Or is the protection limited to &quot;in-house&quot; work? And surely a big problem will come with creating Wonders... if a Wonder is horribly vulgar it will suffer outside yes, but you can create them much more easily.<br /> <br /> - This falls outside RAW, but imagine a Cyborg with 5 points of Permadox is sitting inside of a Laboratory for cybernetics. Cybernetic Genius rolls are 100% coincidental here, along with most scientific stuff. So does the cyborg suffer from Permadox here, or does the Consensus in this space mean that there is nothing paradoxical about the augmentations? I'm imagining a Cyborg working out &quot;malfunctions&quot; (Paradox) inside their Sanctum where it's safer and they can fix themselves more easily (and in game terms, reduce the size of the Paradox pool by 5). Remember that a cyborg with Permadox loses the dox if they remove the relevant augmentations. So clearly the permadox isn't &quot;innate&quot;, but an ongoing backlash against the presence of something that reality rejects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-11-2018, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T18:08:49-07:00","id":1205850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1205830#post1205830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Can a Demesne be someone's Sanctum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically as it relates to magic, they already are. Unless you're using M20's Sanctum rules, there would be no purpose to this, and even with M20's rules it doesn't seem worth the cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, when they are in a Sanctum, a Mage gets hidden by the Arcane effect; if a Mage's sanctum is a space in the dream world that they can access, is it arcane in terms of people trying to find it? And does the Mage become Arcane while they're using it? </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that the mage is effectively existing in two places during this unless they use higher level magic to bodily enter their Demense. As long as their physical body is in the physical world, it can be tracked even if their mind is elsewhere, so they wouldn't benefit from the Arcane bonus for Sanctums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Assuming a Mage has a lot of power over their Demesne (it's their Wellspring, Sanctum and base of operations, and it's also home to a society of Dream-Mind Patterns they created using Mind and Spirit, and they have the lucid dreaming ability at 5 with a spec in Demesne), can it make an effective Mind Prison for enemies? </div> </div> </div>This is too dependent on the relative skills of the mage and the subject they're trying to imprison to really answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering this, doesn't it make a lot of problems just non-issues? </div> </div> </div>Some yes. Though magic that has a constant effect (like giving yourself wings) has to stay in the Sanctum to avoid issues. Healing yourself in your Sanctum would be coincidental, yes. Using Correspondence to cast stuff outside your Sanctum? Not unless it would be coincidental where the spell lands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - This falls outside RAW, but imagine a Cyborg with 5 points of Permadox is sitting inside of a Laboratory for cybernetics. </div> </div> </div>Permadox only had a real effect when the Cyborg invokes Paradox. Permadox is still a threat when effects are coincidental, because coincidental magic can botch and provoke Paradox.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T00:57:06-07:00","id":1205961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1205850#post1205850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Permadox only had a real effect when the Cyborg invokes Paradox. Permadox is still a threat when effects are coincidental, because coincidental magic can botch and provoke Paradox.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but in terms of fluff, the mechanical components of a cyborg only create Permanent Paradox because of their vulgarity; the reality zone may be technologically powerful, but it rejects them, and the pattern can't yet fully bear the weight of them.<br /> <br /> So if you're sitting in a space where such alterations are completely 100% coincidental, then can you ignore the Permanent Paradox temporarily, is my point.<br /> <br /> And thanks for the other answers! I suppose I would add the Arcane rating to attempts to detect the Mage within the dream, if they were hiding in their Demesne and you had broken in, and I'd use it to resist attempts to find their Demesne within the Maya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T01:20:11-07:00","id":1205964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1205830#post1205830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the responses everyone! Cool ideas on the more esoteric stuff not covered in the rules, solid info on the RAW stuff.<br /> <br /> More Questions!<br /> <br /> - Can a Demesne be someone's Sanctum? So I'm imagining someone having a Demesne 5 + Sanctum 5 background where their Memory Palace is extremely powerful and has been shaped to suit their magick. Since Dreams, Invocations, Meditation etc. make up the majority of their foci, the Mage can enter their Demesne while meditating or sleeping and use Magick from inside of it, targeting the real world via Correspondence. Furthermore, when they are in a Sanctum, a Mage gets hidden by the Arcane effect; if a Mage's sanctum is a space in the dream world that they can access, is it arcane in terms of people trying to find it? And does the Mage become Arcane while they're using it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mage residing in his/her demesne would have to use not only Correspondence but also Spirit, because he/she casts spells from outside the borders of physical reality. Sleeping people could be affected more directly, but with the downside that finding a sleeping mind in the Dreaming is pretty hard and probably not worth the effort.<br /> A Sanctum has an Arcane rating, yes. If the Demesne was also the Sanctum, it would profit from the Arcane.<br /> That beeing said, it wouldn't be worth it to make a Demesne your Sanctum as most probably it would already work in your paradigm, so all effects inside the Demesne are already considered coincidental (exept when you have some f***ed up dreams, where the world doesn't work like you think it should).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Assuming a Mage has a lot of power over their Demesne (it's their Wellspring, Sanctum and base of operations, and it's also home to a society of Dream-Mind Patterns they created using Mind and Spirit, and they have the lucid dreaming ability at 5 with a spec in Demesne), can it make an effective Mind Prison for enemies? There's a mechanic for dragging people in; once they're there, can you have the dream completely smother them and present them with Things Man Was Not Meant to See (you don't have to experience those, just drag them from the nightmares of Marauders you've extracted without experiencing perhaps?)? </div> </div> </div>Yeah! Mind prison of hell. I really like this. And it should be totally possible. However, if a prisoner somehow get's out, he would be free to roam your Sanctum. Sure, there'll be security guards you &quot;made up&quot; but depending on how powerfull/smart the escapee is, he could do some damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Sanctums make all of your Paradigm's effects Coincidental. Considering this, doesn't it make a lot of problems just non-issues? Like the 9 point degeneration flaw, which gives you Aggravated damage each fortnight. With a Sanctum, the roll to fix it is pretty standard. Life 3, Coincidental. And what about effects which are only balanced because of how thoroughly vulgar they are? Like reaching out with Correspondence and turning someone into something nasty (assuming this fits the lab/sanctum). Or is the protection limited to &quot;in-house&quot; work? And surely a big problem will come with creating Wonders... if a Wonder is horribly vulgar it will suffer outside yes, but you can create them much more easily. </div> </div> </div>Only in-house effects are coincidental. Everything that effects reality outside of your Sanctum is based on the local reality of where the effect manifests. Creating a horribly vulgar wonder in your Sanctum is a piece of cake, but outside it will quickly generate Paradox as per the rules. That's why Sanctums are so damn cool but still balanced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - This falls outside RAW, but imagine a Cyborg with 5 points of Permadox is sitting inside of a Laboratory for cybernetics. Cybernetic Genius rolls are 100% coincidental here, along with most scientific stuff. So does the cyborg suffer from Permadox here, or does the Consensus in this space mean that there is nothing paradoxical about the augmentations? I'm imagining a Cyborg working out &quot;malfunctions&quot; (Paradox) inside their Sanctum where it's safer and they can fix themselves more easily (and in game terms, reduce the size of the Paradox pool by 5). Remember that a cyborg with Permadox loses the dox if they remove the relevant augmentations. So clearly the permadox isn't &quot;innate&quot;, but an ongoing backlash against the presence of something that reality rejects. </div> </div> </div>I'd rule this exactly like you described the situation. Imagine all the stuff tested in labs and workshops and when they are used in the open space, there's always something going wrong that nobody considered before. That's Permadox building in consensual reality.<br /> Triggering Paradox backlashes inside your Sanctuary, especially when having accrued Permadox, may be a very good idea, indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T02:13:49-07:00","id":1205969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1205964#post1205964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mage residing in his/her demesne would have to use not only Correspondence but also Spirit, because he/she casts spells from outside the borders of physical reality. Sleeping people could be affected more directly, but with the downside that finding a sleeping mind in the Dreaming is pretty hard and probably not worth the effort.<br /> A Sanctum has an Arcane rating, yes. If the Demesne was also the Sanctum, it would profit from the Arcane.<br /> That beeing said, it wouldn't be worth it to make a Demesne your Sanctum as most probably it would already work in your paradigm, so all effects inside the Demesne are already considered coincidental (exept when you have some f***ed up dreams, where the world doesn't work like you think it should).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah! Mind prison of hell. I really like this. And it should be totally possible. However, if a prisoner somehow get's out, he would be free to roam your Sanctum. Sure, there'll be security guards you &quot;made up&quot; but depending on how powerfull/smart the escapee is, he could do some damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Only in-house effects are coincidental. Everything that effects reality outside of your Sanctum is based on the local reality of where the effect manifests. Creating a horribly vulgar wonder in your Sanctum is a piece of cake, but outside it will quickly generate Paradox as per the rules. That's why Sanctums are so damn cool but still balanced.<br /> <br /> <br /> Triggering Paradox backlashes inside your Sanctuary, especially when having accrued Permadox, may be a very good idea, indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good.<br /> <br /> I can see a group of PCs running away from a palace in an NPC's dream...<br /> <br /> &quot;You think you can get away?! You're in MY world!&quot;<br /> <br /> That makes a lot of sense. So you can do your vulgar Werewolf xenotransplants in your lab with fewer problems, but remotely mind-controlling a Werewolf to come and surrender to you (dumb and difficult Mind effect but just an example) won't benefit from the Sanctum's consensus. However, I'm assuming it still benefits from the Difficulty reduction?<br /> <br /> What's the simplest and safest way to trigger a Paradox backlash?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T02:25:08-07:00","id":1205970,"title":"","content":"- If we stack all of our bonuses (Cult, Sanctum, Node etc.) are we able to invoke really horrible effects as defenses? &quot;Anyone who goes past the Ward, who isn't meant to be able to go past it (one of the Wards which distinguish between people using Mind), gets vaporized&quot; kind of defenses. Reading through all of this, I'm finding the idea of a Mage playing on their home turf more and more terrifying.<br /> <br /> - Paradigms which don't fit a Laboratory or Sanctum get vulgar effects; does this apply to literally all effects? It says in M20 that the Black Suit kicking down the door into a witch's sanctum would be at a disadvantage as all of his enlightened procedures would be treated as Vulgar. So this applies to his Dimensional Science / Prime 1 roll to search for Reality Deviants? His Mind 1 roll to sharpen his wits using psychodynamics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T04:40:28-07:00","id":1205985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1205970#post1205970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Paradigms which don't fit a Laboratory or Sanctum get vulgar effects; does this apply to literally all effects? It says in M20 that the Black Suit kicking down the door into a witch's sanctum would be at a disadvantage as all of his enlightened procedures would be treated as Vulgar. So this applies to his Dimensional Science / Prime 1 roll to search for Reality Deviants? His Mind 1 roll to sharpen his wits using psychodynamics?</div> </div> </div> </div>A good guideline is usually &quot;If nobody would notice anything anywhere on Earth, and thus does not use a too obvious mystical or technological focus, it's probably coincidental in any Sanctum.&quot;<br /> Example: If his Mind 1 procedure is him simply focusing in a sort of Mantra or Meditation for a moment, the Mage staring at him in the Sanctum would not notice anything off. He would notice, maybe, that the Black Suit is doing SOMETHING, but Vulgar Without Witnesses would not kick in, because there is nothing noticable wrong about somebody just murmuring to themselves for a moment, no matter where on Earth you are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1205970#post1205970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- If we stack all of our bonuses (Cult, Sanctum, Node etc.) are we able to invoke really horrible effects as defenses? &quot;Anyone who goes past the Ward, who isn't meant to be able to go past it (one of the Wards which distinguish between people using Mind), gets vaporized&quot; kind of defenses. Reading through all of this, I'm finding the idea of a Mage playing on their home turf more and more terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are terrifying. Because when you fight a mage in their Sanctum, you are, literally, fighting inside *their* reality. Their Paradigm rules there, and if the House Flambeau Master decides to lock you in a Correspondence box and drop a Forces nuke on you, it will be coincidental all the way.<br /> <br /> There are a few locations that have similiar feats, and I guess a sort of ranking can be made: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Sanctum</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Advantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">The mage's paradigm rules. Also, if another Mage has the same Paradigm (and paradigmic variation, it should be very very close), it will be also a good place for them.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Disadvantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">That other mage better not be a rival</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Demesne</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Advantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">The mage's paradigm rules. Also, they can more or less shape the realm at will at high ratings of the Demesne background, making them almost a godlike figure.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Disadvantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">The demesne is a dream, literally. It's hard to bring anything physical in there, and the mage's actual body is usually asleep and vulnerable. Best visited while in a Sanctum, or if the mage is inconspicous and has a safe(ish) life.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Shade/shard realm of &lt;Sphere&gt;</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Advantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Holy balls, if your mage has a big affinity for a specific sphere, their according effects might go Full Throttle, potentially with big bonuses.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Disadvantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">So would every other mage's with a big focus (lowercase f) on a specific sphere, and it's not dependant on paradigm. also those realms can be incredibly hazardous.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">General Umbra</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Advantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">A lot of things are coincidental for everyone involved on a base level.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Disadvantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Further coincidence of more powerful effects depends on where you are, which kind of Umbra you are in, and/or what realm you are visiting. Also, the Umbra can be a very hazardous place unless you are a veteran traveller, though to a lesser degree than the Shade- or Shard Realms.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Deep Umbra</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">Advantage:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 4px\">C\u034e\u0347\u0355\u0323\u0325\u032c\u0349\u031fo\u0362\u033b\u0329\u0320\u033a\u0347\u0349\u0332\u0355m\u031e\u0339\u0356\u0317\u032b\u0345\u0320\u0347e\u0327\u0347\u0330\u0354 \u035d\u0348\u0316\u0332\u0320\u032f\u0319a\u035a\u0347t\u0358\u031d \u035c\u035f\u0328\u031f\u0347\u032al\u0336\u031d\u031e\u031e\u032a\u0320\u0316\u032c\u032b\u0329a\u035f\u0327\u0353\u032a\u0348s\u0340\u0340\u0355\u0347\u0319\u031e\u0347\u031f\u031f\u033bt\u035e\u0341\u0332\u035a\u032f\u0355\u032c\u0355 \u0336\u0327\u031f\u0353\u0320\u032b\u0323t\u0338\u0327\u031c\u0349\u031f\u031c\u0353\u0356\u031e\u0323\u033bh\u035c\u032c\u032ae\u035f\u0321\u0349\u033b\u033b\u0347\u0355\u0333\u033c\u032b\u0329 \u035e\u0361\u0315\u032d\u0324\u034d\u033b\u033b\u0349\u0319l\u0362\u031f\u0319\u033a\u0353\u033b\u032e\u033ao\u031f\u0318n\u0315\u0320\u0349\u0355g\u034f\u0335\u0324\u032c\u0317\u0320\u0345 \u032c\u032d\u0353\u031f\u032a\u0324\u0318\u0331f\u0340\u0319\u0355\u034do\u0362\u032c\u0317\u032a\u0319\u0329\u0324\u0326\u0359\u0326r\u0358\u0337\u0347\u032a\u034e\u032d\u032de\u0360\u0315\u0320\u032a\u0329\u0331t\u0489\u0356\u0355o