blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-12-2018, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T06:33:51-07:00","id":1206007,"title":"","content":"Okay, since we're getting out into the Tapestry...<br /> <br /> - Vampires don't seem to have much issue reaching the Shadowlands. With some Necromancy, even other Vampire's Necromancy, any Cainite can step into the shadowlands. And Vampiric Necromancy can, in some rare cases, bring mortals into the Shadowlands. With all of that in mind, why do Mages struggle so much entering the Low Umbra mentally or physically? I'm assuming it's because their bodies are alive, but surely some Life/Entropy will protect them?<br /> <br /> - The Dreaming; can it be entered physically with the right Spheres?<br /> <br /> - Is the Dreaming the same as Arcadia? Can someone with Fae Blood move through the Dreaming more easily?<br /> <br /> - If someone's Demesne is fiercely technological and mundane (their mind palace, dream-space reality construct, REM simulation), with banality pouring out of it, does it become like a tumour within The Dreaming?<br /> <br /> - Can Fae invade someone's Demesne?<br /> <br /> - Dream-linked Mages who are unusually adept; will they attract Changelings?<br /> <br /> And back to Nodes...<br /> <br /> - Gaian creatures fiercely defend their Cairns. Is there a means through which Mages and Werewolves (etc.) can happily share a Node? When a Mage draws Quintessence from a Node, do they profane it in the eyes of the Garou? Is there a mechanical downside to sharing it, or is it all down to prejudice, mistrust, hatred and past experience? I mean a reality-warping stranger who wishes to use your sacred site will always be a big issue, but I'm assuming there will be exceptions. Kinfolk Mages, Mages with Paradigms that suit the Shifters...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T07:21:50-07:00","id":1206015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1206007#post1206007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, since we're getting out into the Tapestry...<br /> <br /> - Vampires don't seem to have much issue reaching the Shadowlands. With some Necromancy, even other Vampire's Necromancy, any Cainite can step into the shadowlands. And Vampiric Necromancy can, in some rare cases, bring mortals into the Shadowlands. With all of that in mind, why do Mages struggle so much entering the Low Umbra mentally or physically? I'm assuming it's because their bodies are alive, but surely some Life/Entropy will protect them?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Demon Lore, the Lower Umbra was sealed in a way so it wouldn't be found and can't be entered by living beings.<br /> The reason in a pure mage setting would be, that mages are alive. There are the Soujourn-Spells to enter the Lower Umbra as a spirit while leaving your living body behind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The Dreaming; can it be entered physically with the right Spheres?<br /> <br /> - Is the Dreaming the same as Arcadia? Can someone with Fae Blood move through the Dreaming more easily? </div> </div> </div>The Dreaming would most likely be accessed via the Higher Umbra, when traveling through the umbra. However there are also connections to the shenti (like the Malfeas). There are ways to travel into the Umbra physically and thus, it should be possible to go into the Dreaming from there.<br /> Arcadia is (in Changeling) a lost part of the Dreaming. It is cut of from the trods that make places in the Dreaming accessible. It's not the same, only a legend of the Changelings. (Dark Ages suggests it's more likely to be the world as it was before the Shattering.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - If someone's Demesne is fiercely technological and mundane (their mind palace, dream-space reality construct, REM simulation), with banality pouring out of it, does it become like a tumour within The Dreaming? </div> </div> </div>To be this infected by Banality, one has to be a Dauntain or worse. I don't believe your connection to the Dreaming would be strong enough to establish a Demesne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Can Fae invade someone's Demesne?<br /> <br /> - Dream-linked Mages who are unusually adept; will they attract Changelings? </div> </div> </div>Fae raiding parties on your Demesne? Hell yeah. That's probably possible and it would be a lot of fun for a storyteller.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And back to Nodes...<br /> <br /> - Gaian creatures fiercely defend their Cairns. Is there a means through which Mages and Werewolves (etc.) can happily share a Node? When a Mage draws Quintessence from a Node, do they profane it in the eyes of the Garou? Is there a mechanical downside to sharing it, or is it all down to prejudice, mistrust, hatred and past experience? I mean a reality-warping stranger who wishes to use your sacred site will always be a big issue, but I'm assuming there will be exceptions. Kinfolk Mages, Mages with Paradigms that suit the Shifters... </div> </div> </div>Werewolves see caerns as holy places. It's Gaias energy flowing out of them. Simply taking it for yourself is not only profane, it's a sacrilege.<br /> The energy belongs to the spirits, to the world itself. Maybe, if a mage really gains the trust of the werewolves, they may allow it once or twice, if it's for a cause they also believe in. Maybe, if the mage is kinfolk, she has better chances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T07:48:25-07:00","id":1206021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1206015#post1206015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves see caerns as holy places. It's Gaias energy flowing out of them. Simply taking it for yourself is not only profane, it's a sacrilege.<br /> The energy belongs to the spirits, to the world itself. Maybe, if a mage really gains the trust of the werewolves, they may allow it once or twice, if it's for a cause they also believe in. Maybe, if the mage is kinfolk, she has better chances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm seeing a Gaian Kinfolk Mage with bothersome relatives...<br /> <br /> &quot;James. You've brought these... these sorcerers here, again? To our most sacred-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's important. I needed to cleanse my friend of a Demon mum, I thought it would be easier here-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What are they doing messing around with banes?! If your father were here he would-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;IT'S A DEMON MUM. THEY'RE DIFFERENT.&quot;<br /> <br /> - In terms of the mechanical benefits of Nodes, an industrial game recommends that a Node gives 2 points of Quintessence per week, per dot of Node. So a Level 2 Node might produce 2 raw Quintessence each week, and the most beautiful orchids there might add up to 2 points of Tass, each week. Someone with an Avatar can meditate (or equivalent) and draw in points to refuel themselves. I'm assuming that using Prime, someone can draw extra Quintessence out of a Node? That's what tapping a wellspring is, correct? So what's the limit there? How far can you push a Node? Do you risk damaging it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T07:55:33-07:00","id":1206024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason in a pure mage setting would be, that mages are alive. There are the Soujourn-Spells to enter the Lower Umbra as a spirit while leaving your living body behind.</div> </div> </div> </div> Void Engineers can travel bodily by using Life 4 instead of 3, as per their book, by adopting a form loaded with entropic energy. There's also a Merit that makes you resonate with death and lets you step sideways into the dark umbra with Spirit 3 alone. <br /> <br /> Presumably adopting any temporary half-dead or death-related state would also work. I don't think Sojourn it's the only way. It's just an example of how to go there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T08:13:40-07:00","id":1206029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1206021#post1206021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- In terms of the mechanical benefits of Nodes, an industrial game recommends that a Node gives 2 points of Quintessence per week, per dot of Node. So a Level 2 Node might produce 2 raw Quintessence each week, and the most beautiful orchids there might add up to 2 points of Tass, each week. Someone with an Avatar can meditate (or equivalent) and draw in points to refuel themselves. I'm assuming that using Prime, someone can draw extra Quintessence out of a Node? That's what tapping a wellspring is, correct? So what's the limit there? How far can you push a Node? Do you risk damaging it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Prime you draw a lot faster. You can draw extra Quintessence but then you're damaging the Node for sure, though I don't quite remember the limits.<br /> <br /> That's not what tapping a wellspring is. A Wellspring it's a temporary surge of Quintessence that sometimes get's released as response of a very strong ressonance (which can be forced by Mage with Prime 4 - if you have Prime 4 and find a place charged with strong emotions you can generate a Quint flow there)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-12-2018, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T08:14:38-07:00","id":1206030,"title":"","content":"I also vaguely recall there being a Rote in one of the Dead Magic books, that allowed a mage to enter the Shadowlands with just Spirit 3. It was described as being something possible because of the original culture's different outlook on the underworld, which may or may not work for other mages. It may also be that the ancient culture existed in a time where the spiritual make-up of the world was sufficiently different that one COULD just cross over to the land of the dead as one could cross over to any other part of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would imagine it's possible for someone to use something other than the Sojourn to go to the Shadowlands. It's just difficult, and methods for doing so would require jumping through a few extra hoops. It's worth keeping in mind that while we like to think of the Umbra as one huge place with consistent rules, it's actually made up of different broad categories with their own quirks and requirements. You can't really get very far in the High Umbra, for instance, without using Mind instead of Spirit. So the Low Umbra have similarly specific prerequisites seems reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T08:22:59-07:00","id":1206033,"title":"","content":"I remember seeing someone on these forums mention a Life 3 Verbena rote which upgrades a Node by sacrificing a living person (willing, I think?) to the Node. But it was back when I barely understood Mage, so I can't remember the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:30:35-07:00","id":1206045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1206033#post1206033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember seeing someone on these forums mention a Life 3 Verbena rote which upgrades a Node by sacrificing a living person (willing, I think?) to the Node. But it was back when I barely understood Mage, so I can't remember the specifics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Verbena rote you're talking about was a ritual to flood the land with the Quintessence of said sacrifice to heal the life on it. It wasn't designed to upgrade Nodes. Also yes, it had to be a willing sacrifice or the violent resonances of unwillingly given Quintessence would have tainted the land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:51:11-07:00","id":1206052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1206045#post1206045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Verbena rote you're talking about was a ritual to flood the land with the Quintessence of said sacrifice to heal the life on it. It wasn't designed to upgrade Nodes. Also yes, it had to be a willing sacrifice or the violent resonances of unwillingly given Quintessence would have tainted the land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Strange that it isn't using Prime too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T15:16:54-07:00","id":1206175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1205961#post1205961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but in terms of fluff, the mechanical components of a cyborg only create Permanent Paradox because of their vulgarity; the reality zone may be technologically powerful, but it rejects them, and the pattern can't yet fully bear the weight of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the thread kinda moved on, but I figured I'd address this. Permadox is already part of the subject's Pattern. If something causes it, the Paradox energies in their Pattern are so strong it doesn't matter any more. The only way to avoid the increased potency of backlashes is to purge yourself of the source of the Permadox. You can't ignore Permadox, ever, no matter the dominant Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> Think of it kind of like &quot;reality damage.&quot; If I take four lethal damage, it doesn't matter what Reality Zones I travel to, it's always four lethal damage with the penalties that implies. Different Reality Zones can only impact how I deal with that damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T22:49:17-07:00","id":1206294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1206033#post1206033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember seeing someone on these forums mention a Life 3 Verbena rote which upgrades a Node by sacrificing a living person (willing, I think?) to the Node. But it was back when I barely understood Mage, so I can't remember the specifics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you thinking of the Verbena Revised &quot;Sacred King&quot; rote? It's Prime 3, and releases all the Quint of a willing sacrificial victim, or, if the sacrifice is an Awakened mage, can upgrade a Node.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:25:46-07:00","id":1207032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1206175#post1206175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know the thread kinda moved on, but I figured I'd address this. Permadox is already part of the subject's Pattern. If something causes it, the Paradox energies in their Pattern are so strong it doesn't matter any more. The only way to avoid the increased potency of backlashes is to purge yourself of the source of the Permadox. You can't ignore Permadox, ever, no matter the dominant Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> Think of it kind of like &quot;reality damage.&quot; If I take four lethal damage, it doesn't matter what Reality Zones I travel to, it's always four lethal damage with the penalties that implies. Different Reality Zones can only impact how I deal with that damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's &quot;reality damage&quot; then that doesn't explain how removing a bit of cyborg tech (like your implanted internet access in the back of your neck) removes the Permadox. The two are intrinsically linked, I believe, in V20. You get the Permadox because you have installed something (whether it's a second ago, or a year ago) which the reality zone can't fully handle. Your very pattern is being rejected, slightly.<br /> <br /> So if someone enters a Realm where Technomagick is 100% coincidental, or a Laboratory for the Technocracy or the VAs or the SoE, then I can only think of their onboard internet access which meshes with their brain (something that tech can't achieve in our world yet, hence the rejection, even if it might be normal unenlightened tech in 30 years) as being something that entirely fits within reality when they enter that space. Your example of damage is also weird, since if they were to remove the paradoxical installment and put it back in while they were in the Lab, by your interpretation of the rules they would get the Permadox back, which doesn't fit with your logic; clearly they're not just carrying damage to their Pattern from the universe rejecting it with them. It's constant low-level rejection since no reality zone agrees with them. Except the reality zone where nothing they do within their paradigm is ever Vulgar? Like their Lab. You see what I'm getting at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:43:32-07:00","id":1207108,"title":"","content":"OK, in the damage analogy (which yes, isn't perfect) taking it out is healing the damage, and putting it back it is doing the damage again.<br /> <br /> Enhancements cause Permadox regardless of the Reality Zone you're in, so why it happens isn't dependent on where you do it. Getting an Enhancement in a Technocratic facility causes the same Permadox as doing it in a normal hospital. Doing it in a proper Laboratory only reduces the risk of Paradox for the installation. Hanging out in friendly Realty Zones reduces the dangers of Permadox because you need to botch magic rolls for it to matter if you stick in a safe spot.<br /> <br /> I get that it might not make complete sense, but that's the way the game is set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T23:29:34-07:00","id":1207183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1207108#post1207108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, in the damage analogy (which yes, isn't perfect) taking it out is healing the damage, and putting it back it is doing the damage again.<br /> <br /> Enhancements cause Permadox regardless of the Reality Zone you're in, so why it happens isn't dependent on where you do it. Getting an Enhancement in a Technocratic facility causes the same Permadox as doing it in a normal hospital. Doing it in a proper Laboratory only reduces the risk of Paradox for the installation. Hanging out in friendly Realty Zones reduces the dangers of Permadox because you need to botch magic rolls for it to matter if you stick in a safe spot.<br /> <br /> I get that it might not make complete sense, but that's the way the game is set up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would argue that the Permadox shouldn't happen if the person with the enhancements does not leave the technomagickal reality zone. The same way how giving yourself inhuman enhancements in a mystic reality zone shouldn't. The reason it is paradoxial is, after all, based on consensus.<br /> <br /> However, if you ever leave it, permadox strikes. I''d personally consider it turning into normal paradox while being in an according reality zone again though. Which also means it can be purged or go away over time (though it should not instantly vanish). However, as soon as you leave the according zone once more, it returns as permadox.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I'd handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-15-2018, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T01:32:48-07:00","id":1207200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1205626-questions-on-nodes?p=1207183#post1207183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I would argue that the Permadox shouldn't happen if the person with the enhancements does not leave the technomagickal reality zone. The same way how giving yourself inhuman enhancements in a mystic reality zone shouldn't. The reason it is paradoxial is, after all, based on consensus.<br /> <br /> However, if you ever leave it, permadox strikes. I''d personally consider it turning into normal paradox while being in an according reality zone again though. Which also means it can be purged or go away over time (though it should not instantly vanish). However, as soon as you leave the according zone once more, it returns as permadox.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I'd handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And for a cyborg, shifting the Consensus to accept cyborgs will be a big deal! Imagine if their 3 P-D enhancements, thanks to legitimate scientific advances and PR moves by the Technocrats, gradually became more acceptable and only gave him 1 or 2 dots of P-D. Now they can enjoy that added safety, or add another enhancement to their body.<br /> <br /> Imagine what Iteration X could do if their plasma weapons were BARELY coincidental, in most parts of the world, meaning that their Primium Countermeasures are the only part that is rejected. Imagine what they could load up onto their patterns in addition, to meet the same amount of Permadox. Healing nanites. A short-range teleporter. A stealth field. It's just another reason for them to fight in the Ascension War and push people towards accepting hypertech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-15-2018, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T06:08:56-07:00","id":1207235,"title":"","content":"OK, I'm trying to help clarify what the books actually say. If you want to house rule it, go for it, but this isn't a case of the game being unclear on what it says how things &quot;should be.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}